MS (Mad Shift) quantization for llama.cpp
Copyright (c) 2026 Matthew Priester (https://github.com/devvexus, ORCID 0009-0000-0032-5292)

This fork of llama.cpp adds the MS (Mad Shift) weight format, written by Matthew Priester:
- the MS_C1..MS_C6 tensor types (bitshift-trellis code, k = 1..6 bits per weight, 512-weight blocks) and their CPU (x86, ARM)
  and CUDA kernels;
- the prism.hadamard input-rotation metadata and its handling in the graph;
- split embedding tables and split output heads (msffn.emb_split_order, output_lo).

The trellis code builds on QTIP (A. Tseng, Q. Sun, D. Hou, C. De Sa, "QTIP: Quantization with Trellises and Incoherence
Processing", NeurIPS 2024, arXiv:2406.11235): the bitshift trellis and its computed "1MAD" decoder.

